  "summary": "The streamer shares a lengthy personal anecdote about a chaotic experience in Beijing airport, losing a passport, navigating without internet or translation tools, dealing with police, and ultimately boarding a flight with a handwritten ticket. No game‑related predictions or team commentary are made in these turns.",
  "takes": [
    {
      "at_ms": 183620,
      "subject": "general",
      "take": "I think it's not going to be a problem. I think it's a problem. It's a problem. I think it's very important to them. I think it's a good time for the last two weeks. So, I think it's a good time for the last two weeks. I'm not going to lose."
    },
    {
      "at_ms": 199060,
      "subject": "general",
      "take": "You have? You lost your passport there? Well, no. It doesn't really count. I was taking a connecting flight. That's basically what happened."
    },
    {
      "at_ms": 214680,
      "subject": "general",
      "take": "That story is wild though. Oh my god. That was my only experience in China, is taking a connecting flight in Beijing at fucking 3 in the morning. When my flight's at 6, the airport was empty, literally empty. Everything was in Chinese. I couldn't use my data. I couldn't open up any social media platforms. I couldn't..."
    },
    {
      "at_ms": 236880,
      "subject": "general",
      "take": "I couldn't open up any translate, nothing. I didn't have any connection to anything. And the only way I could get there is finding two police officers, asking them where my flight was, because I couldn't find a table that said, like, flight connections or anything. And I was with a homie, and it was for, um..."
    },
    {
      "at_ms": 252180,
      "subject": "general",
      "take": "We were going to Korea in 2023, uh, and I found two police officers, and they, they... they asked me to show me my passport, I showed them my passport, and then they, they got their phone out, took a picture of my passport, and put it in a WeChat group, and then they left..."
    },
    {
      "at_ms": 270380,
      "subject": "general",
      "take": "and then they came back like 30 minutes later, and they fucking took me around the back of the airport, to like a police scanning zone, they like ripped through all of my suitcase, clothes, everything, and then once I had everything back, they then took me on a bus to the other side of the airport, and when I entered the other side of the airport, there was people there,"
    },
    {
      "at_ms": 295300,
      "subject": "general",
      "take": "and then I was like, bro, what about my ticket? Then they gave me a piece of paper, and they wrote something in Chinese on my piece of paper, and with my name and my seat number, they just gave me a written piece of paper and said, here's your ticket. So then I went to the flight, and I just gave them this fucking piece of paper, and they looked at me so weird,"
    },
    {
      "at_ms": 311720,
      "subject": "general",
      "take": "and they let me on the plane. That was my only experience in China. Yes, I came very unprepared. I didn't have any VPN, I didn't know how to use any fucking translate shit or anything, because my idea, okay, my idea was,"
    },
    {
      "at_ms": 328380,
      "subject": "general",
      "take": "why don't I just leave the airport and come back in and check in? That was my idea. Sounds smart, right? As I went to leave, you needed to show your COVID pass, because it was still quite soon after COVID, but I didn't have internet to do it, and there was, like, people wearing hazmat suits, and I was like, oh, fuck this."
    },
    {
      "at_ms": 345960,
      "subject": "general",
      "take": "There's no way I'm getting back in or leaving this airport, this is gonna be full chopped if I do that. I only had it on, there was, like, an app called Cove Pass or some shit, and it just wasn't updating."
    }
  ],
  "teams": ["RED Kalunga", "FlyQuest"]
}

